# Frozen experimental inputs must reach every model byte for byte.
#
# Without this, a checkout on Windows with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every
# LF to CRLF, and the prompts stop matching the sha256 recorded in their
# manifest at build time. That is not cosmetic: it silently breaks the one
# guarantee the whole design rests on, that the prompt bytes are identical
# across conditions and across models. Marking these trees -text tells git
# never to translate them, on any platform.
tsrbench50/cli/**       -text
tsrbench160/cli/**      -text
out_paper50_reviewed/** -text
sanity/cli/**           -text
prompts/**              -text

# The frozen source data and the manifests that pin the prompt hashes.
tsrbench50/*.jsonl      -text
tsrbench50/*.json       -text
tsrbench160/*.jsonl     -text
tsrbench160/*.json      -text

# Results are the record of what happened and are hashed and compared too.
results/**              -text

# Everything else: store LF in the repository, and check it out as LF, so a
# script written on one machine runs unchanged on the other.
*                       text=auto eol=lf
